==English==

===Pronunciation===
*: {{rhymes|æməl}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fr}} {{term|tramail||net for catching fishes}}, from {{etyl|LL.}} {{term|tremaculum}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# Something that [[impede]]s [[activity]], [[freedom]], or [[progress]].
#* {{quote-book|year=1898|year_published=1911|author=[[s:Author:William Graham Sumner|William Graham Sumner]]|title=[[s:War and Other Essays|War and Other Essays]]|chapter=[[s:The Conquest of the United States by Spain|The Conquest of the United States by Spain]]|publisher=Yale|page=[[s:Page:War and Other Essays.djvu/368|332]]|passage=The men who came here were able to throw off all the '''trammels''' of tradition and established doctrine.}}
# A [[fishing]] [[net]] that has large [[mesh]] at the edges and smaller mesh in the middle
# A set of [[ring]]s or other hanging devices, attached to a transverse bar suspended over a [[fire]], used to hang [[cooking pot]]s etc.

